  "lyrics": "1. Twinkle, twinkle little star, how I wonder what you are! up above the world so high, like a diamond in the sky. Twinkle, twinkle little star, how I wonder what you are!",
  "notes": [
   "Curriculum song (Prep A, prep-a.skips). Words Jane Taylor (1806), traditional tune; public domain. Our own arrangement in Middle C position, the tune shared between the hands (in G, with no F sharp). The M1 test song (arch §12). Chord symbols (G, C, D) for the backing (Oct 7, 2026): without them it took its chords from the left hand alone, and stopped whenever the tune was in the right hand."
  ],
